(instances (project "panel-interface" (path "/3245cefd-46fb-5f7c-ba88-7a6f60142abf" (reference "H2") (unit 1)))))
(text "NOTES\n1. Normal = loop closed: coil on, NO closed, GPIO = 3.3 V (reads 1). Alarm, power loss or cut cable = GPIO 0.\n2. The FP2 D3009 coil is 5 V (178R, limit 11 V) and POLARIZED: pin 1 +, pin 10 -. R1/R2 drop 12 V to about 4.8 V.\n3. 3V3 comes from the Pi, so a GPIO never sees voltage while the Pi is off.\n4. Relay LEDs run from 3.3 V: use red, orange or yellow (forward voltage up to 2.2 V). Blue or white will not light.\n5. R9/R10 pull down harder than a leftover Pi pull-up. R7/R8 protect the GPIO from wiring mistakes.\n6. F1/F2: a short on the panel cable trips only that line, so the Pi and modem stay powered and can report it.\n7. The PANEL LED cannot tell an alarm from an unplugged cable: both open the loop." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 148.59 30.48 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "5e1bb375-9560-5acd-bc91-c3cce8ead9c1"))
